meta {
  name: 01 Issue Patient Credentials
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}/login-credentials
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  const data = body && body.data;
  if (data && data.loginIdentifier) {
    bru.setEnvVar("patientLoginIdentifier", data.loginIdentifier);
  }
}

docs {
  **Staff action (business JWT).** Enables patient-portal login for a patient.

  - Links the patient to a platform `Person` (creates/links one when the patient
    row has no `personId`), creates a `PersonCredentials` row with the fixed temp
    password **`Password@123`** (bcrypt-hashed, `isTempPassword = true`), and
    records a `PersonTenantEnrollment` — the platform index patient login reads to
    list the patient's businesses.
  - Tenant + actor come from the JWT; nothing is taken from the body (there is no
    body). `:id` is the tenant-scoped patient id.
  - **Idempotent on an existing login:** if the person already has credentials
    (e.g. a staff+patient hybrid) they are kept — `tempPassword` is `null` and
    `credentialsAlreadyExisted = true`. Use **Reset Patient Password** to force the
    temp password.

  Response `data`: `{ patientId, personId, loginIdentifier, tempPassword,
  credentialsAlreadyExisted }`. Captures `patientLoginIdentifier`.

  Errors: `404 PATIENT_NOT_FOUND` (not in tenant); `422
  PATIENT_HAS_NO_LOGIN_IDENTIFIER` (patient has no mobile/email); `401` without a
  business token.
}
